# env: MNML_PROFILE=dev
# The dev profile says so on the statusline. One machine runs two
# mnmls — the installed one you live in and the build you are working
# on — and the only thing telling them apart on screen is this chip
# beside the mode (`src/app/statusline.zig`, `src/config/profile.zig`).
# The window title carries the same tag, which a screen dump cannot
# see; `tools/run-sh-check.sh` covers the rest of the profile's names.
#
# The stable profile paints nothing at all — every other script in this
# corpus runs in it and none of them show a `dev`, which is the other
# half of this assertion.
write hello.txt "hi"
open hello.txt
expect screen contains "dev"
expect screen contains "hello.txt"
